{"kind":"assert","text":"dap-demo part 1 Source assessment by checker session 44e8, before the gate. This is not the formal review. Commit 35daa79130de96424e7b9e8802c6036da68a3037 (tree 7ae39904c0cdcc74b499b47543aa379fb40308ec) on Main 27abf6d9, plus seal commit 9a99e2cc3e42b7ea2236e456b89f4b686c6c301f (tree e8551de2, scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs only, two seal values). I read the primary note first, then all 12 paths from Git. The packet a25d7571 copies match the commit blobs byte for byte (12 of 12).\n\nNo required finding. Request witnesses: demo-register.test.ts pairs one outsider key under open (accepted, directory@16 indexed at genesis in enforce mode, unknown sibling scope not-found) with the same key under keys (refused, unauthorized). The CLI test covers invalid policy, a conflicting cohort, a policy conflict on --planned and --plan (plan kept, nothing sent), and planned and direct delivery. Register17 accepts policy open (register.ts:298).\n\nArchitecture: the policy is signed into the retained install intent and fixed to Register17 by object identity. A conflict refuses and keeps the plan. Omission keeps keys and the legacy path. Clear.\nSecurity: the runbook sets the DEPLOYMENT and SESSION_SECRET secrets before the first code deploy. This order is required: creation-admission.ts:19 opens admission when DEPLOYMENT is unset. The new config has no ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION, no DEMO_START_CONFIG, its own namespaces, and the index in enforce mode.\nSimplification: the hard-coded old-origin guard in demo-creation.ts is the smallest change that keeps the retained GitHub authority. Acceptable.\n\nThree nonblocking points for the head report:\nP3-1 (request item 4). On artroom-scope the Start form still shows. Only after submit does the Page say \"This service is not set up to create rooms. Nothing was sent.\" (page/src/main.ts:773). There is no link to dap-demo. This equals the effect of the \"remove DEMO_START_CONFIG\" option the request allows, but the request also asks for a link. State this in the primary so the planner can accept it or ask for a notice.\nP3-2. dap-demo has no APPLICATION_CONTENT bucket or APPLICATION_TRUST, so application fetch and admit answer unavailable (applications/route.ts:61, wiring.ts:19). Rooms there cannot install applications. Name this limit.\nP3-3. ARTIFACTS_CONFIG is given only by --var at deploy. A later deploy without the same --var drops it. Either record the planned nonsecret value in the file after planning, as Grow does, or say in the runbook that every deploy must repeat it.\n\nThe formal review waits for the review request at the exact gated head."}